From 4b96ed21a69487dbdad03d7ec4de5d11af71c5cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:11:08 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] A shrunken building's torches cast shrunken pools: the look's
 torch light follows its host's scale

Elwynn Survival puts Elwynn's own buildings in the camp at a fraction of their size (the Watchtower
is `HumanWatchTower.m2` at a third, the Guard Tower `HumanGuardTower.m2` at two fifths). Those
models carry four wall torches, each an M2 point light of colour (1.0, 0.86, 0.5) with an authored
reach under 2 yd, which the entity path spawns as carried lights. The new look (patch 0057) turned
every authored light into a full torch's pool, 10 yd across at about 1.5 of its strength, whatever
the object's scale: on a tower 7 yd a side the four pools lay over each other on its own pale
stone, the walls took two or three times their own colour and went white from the door to the
roof, and the yard around it lit up torch-yellow for 8 yd. Elwynn's full-size towers show the same
four torches a long stride apart on a wall three times as big, where it reads as a lit doorway.

`look::lights::torch_light` now takes the world scale of what carries the light (the light's
`GlobalTransform`, packed by `build_light_data`), and a host below full size shrinks the pool the
same way, in reach and in strength: a two-fifths tower's torch casts a 4 yd pool at two fifths of
a torch's strength, a candle to a torch. Nothing grows past a full torch's pool, however big its
host, so a planted arrow's glow (scale 1.5) and every placed lamp, brazier and WMO light are as
they were.

Tests: `an_authored_light_becomes_a_pool` covers the 0.42 host (radius and strength two fifths,
the hue its own) and a 2.5 host (a full torch's), and the packer's tests carry the new field.
Filmed on the test server's camp (always 23:30): a Watchtower built at the campfire, before and
after.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
